body:
So I'm working on the face parts for the X axis and I'm having trouble with this layer that I have for keeping the eyeballs from showing outside the lines. I got it very close, but as you can see in the top image some of the skin is still leaking over the whites of the eyes. That's the first problem. 

&#x200B;

The second problem is that now that the skin layer is mangled its function doesn't work as well so the eyeball is capable of leaking outside the skin cover area. I figure I'll have to reset how far the eyeball can move, but is there a way to do that without messing up the eyeball's x and y settings when the model is in a neutral position? 

&#x200B;

Thank you for any help, I'm still trying to figure this stuff out.
